      "name": "LoadExcelTableData",
      "signature": "int * LoadExcelTableData(void * this, int nArchive, byte * pbTableName, void * pFieldDefs, int * pnRowCount, int nRowSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "int *",
      "comment": "Loads Excel table data from either binary cache or text file.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Build file path: DATA\\GLOBAL\\EXCEL\\{tableName}.{txt|bin}\n2. Special case: if tableName matches \"leveldefs\", use \"levels\" instead\n3. Load file data via FUN_6f913fa2\n4. If text mode (g_fUseBinaryExcelData=0):\n   a. Parse tab-delimited text to cell data\n   b. Get row count from parsed data\n   c. Allocate zeroed buffer (rowCount * rowSize)\n   d. Populate table via PopulateExcelTableFromText\n   e. Free parsed cell data\n5. If binary mode: read row count and data pointer directly from buffer\n\nParameters:\n- this (void*): Table loader context (ECX)\n- nArchive (int): MPQ archive handle\n- pbTableName (byte*): Table name string (e.g., \"levels\")\n- pFieldDefs (void*): Field definition structure for parsing\n- pnRowCount (int*): OUT - receives number of table rows\n- nRowSize (int): Size of each table row in bytes\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to allocated/loaded table data, NULL on failure",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
