      "name": "InitCompositeUnitWeapon",
      "signature": "void InitCompositeUnitWeapon(CompositeUnit * pCompositeUnit, uint dwWeaponClassInput, int dwMode, byte * pbComponentData, char * szComponentColors)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initialize CompositeUnit with weapon components and color data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input CompositeUnit pointer\n2. Allocate color buffer via FogMemAlloc(4)\n3. Set weapon class; lookup composite weapon class if class < 7\n4. Initialize component flag bits (multiple bitwise operations on unit state)\n5. Loop through 16 components: fetch component data, remap indices\n6. Copy color string data to unit structure (up to 16 bytes)\n7. Load composite unit graphics via LoadCompositeUnitCof()\n8. Apply composite mode via SetCompositeMode()\n\nParameters:\n- pCompositeUnit (CompositeUnit*): Target unit structure (offset+0xb8=buffer, +0x1c=class, +0x24=composite, +0x20=mode)\n- nWeaponClass (uint): Weapon class index (0-7 range)\n- dwMode (uint): Composite mode flags\n- pbComponentData (byte*): Component type array (16 bytes)\n- szComponentColors (char*): Color string array (up to 16 bytes)\n\nReturns:\n- void; initializes structure in-place and applies graphics\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xb8: Color buffer offset in CompositeUnit\n- 0x1c: Weapon class field offset\n- 0x24: Composite class field offset\n- 0x20: Mode flags field offset\n- 0x38: Component table start offset (offset 0x38, stride 0x4)\n- 0x40: Component duration field offset (+0x40 per entry)\n- 0x7: Weapon class range check boundary\n- 0x10: 16 components per unit maximum",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:b1db912f6d60d5330df107673e91e8c6",
