      "name": "SelectListNodeByGridPosition",
      "signature": "int SelectListNodeByGridPosition(int * * ppListData)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Selects a linked list node based on calculated grid position from screen coordinates.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Dereference ppListData to get actual unit/list data pointer\n2. Assert type field equals 0xc (list data type validation)\n3. Check bitmask flags at offset 0x8 - both visibility and enabled bits must be set\n4. If linked list at offset 0x40 is empty, return 0 (no selection possible)\n5. Calculate target grid index from screen position:\n   - Row = (g_nScreenHeight - unitY) / 120  (120 pixels per row)\n   - Col = ((unitWidth - unitX) + 4 + g_nScreenWidth) / 20  (20 pixels per column)\n   - Index = Row + Col * 6  (6 rows per column)\n6. Walk linked list (next pointer at offset 0x34) until index reached\n7. Store selected node at offset 0x44 (or 0 if list exhausted)\n8. Return 1 on success, 0 if conditions not met\n\nParameters:\n- ppListData: Pointer to pointer to list data structure (type 0xc)\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Successfully selected a node (or cleared selection if list exhausted)\n- 0: Conditions not met (flags not set or no list)\n\nStructure Layout (ListData at *ppListData):\nOffset  Size  Field           Description\n0x00    4     dwType          Must be 0xc for list data\n0x08    4     dwFlags         Bitmask flags (visibility/enabled)\n0x0c    4     nUnitY          Y coordinate for row calculation\n0x10    4     nUnitX          X coordinate\n0x18    4     nUnitWidth      Width for column calculation\n0x40    4     pListHead       Head of linked list (nodes)\n0x44    4     pSelectedNode   Currently selected node (output)\n\nLinked List Node (at offset 0x34 is next pointer):\n- Each node is 0x38+ bytes\n- Offset 0x34: pNextNode pointer\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xc: List data type identifier\n- 0x78 (120): Grid row height in pixels\n- 0x14 (20): Grid column width in pixels\n- 6: Number of rows per column in grid layout",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
