      "name": "CreateGameObject",
      "signature": "void * CreateGameObject(uint dwValue1, uint dwValue2, uint dwValue3, uint dwValue4, uint dwValue5, uint dwValue6, uint dwValue7, int nInitParam, int nDefaultValue, uint dwValue10)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void *",
      "comment": "Allocates and initializes a game object structure (96 bytes).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 96-byte block via FogMemAlloc\n2. Zero-initialize all fields via loop\n3. Set base flags in fields [0] and [2] with bitmask values\n4. Populate object fields from parameters\n5. Link function pointers for callbacks\n6. Call initialization callback FUN_6f90ea50\n\nParameters:\n- dwValue1 (uint): Field [3] value\n- dwValue2 (uint): Field [4] value\n- dwValue3 (uint): Field [5] value\n- dwValue4 (uint): Field [6] value\n- dwValue5 (uint): Field [1] value\n- dwValue6 (uint): Field [0x11] value\n- dwValue7 (uint): Field [0xd] value\n- nInitParam (int): Determines callback population at field [0xe]\n- nDefaultValue (int): Defaults to 5, stored in field [0x15]\n- dwValue10 (uint): Field [0x16] value\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to allocated and initialized 96-byte structure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x60 (96): Structure size in bytes\n- 0x18 (24): Loop count for 24 dword zero-initialization\n- Field [0] is set to 2 (structure type marker)\n- Field [0x12] populated with GetTickCount() timestamp",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
