      "comment": "Renders an animated game object by managing animation state, frame timing, and cel drawing.\n\nClassification: Worker function (render callback for type 2 game objects)\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate object type == 2, assert failure if not\n2. Zero-initialize 0x12 dwords of local CelFileInfo array\n3. Early exit with success (1) if no cel data (field[1]) and no anim table (field[0x10])\n4. Cache position from fields[3] (X) and [4] (Y)\n5. If animation table exists (field[0x10] != 0):\n   a. Get animation mode from field[0x14]\n   b. If mode is 0 or 1, validate cel bounds and update mode\n   c. If mode changed, invoke optional callback at field[0x16]\n   d. Get frame count from current animation entry\n   e. Handle animation state transitions:\n      - State 2: If at end, reset to frame 0 and transition to state 3\n      - State 4: If at end, reset to frame 0 and transition to state 1\n   f. Reset timestamp via GetTickCount on state transition\n   g. Clamp frame index to valid range\n6. Load cel pointers:\n   a. If no anim table: use field[1] as single cel, adjust position by cel dimensions\n   b. If anim table: index by (field[0x10] + field[0x14] * 0x10) for primary/secondary cels\n7. Render primary cel via GfxInterfaceCall84 if present\n8. Render secondary cel via GfxInterfaceCall84 if present\n9. Update frame animation based on elapsed time:\n   a. Calculate frame duration: (direction * 1000) / 25 ms per frame\n   b. For states 2/4: linear frame progression clamped to max\n   c. For other states: looping frame calculation via modulo\n\nParameters:\n- pAnimObject (int * via ECX): Pointer to 96-byte game object structure\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Always returns success\n\nGame Object Structure Layout (offsets in dwords):\nOffset  Size  Field              Description\n0x00    4     dwType             Type identifier (must be 2)\n0x01    4     pCelFile           Single cel file pointer (when no anim table)\n0x03    4     dwPosX             X coordinate\n0x04    4     dwPosY             Y coordinate\n0x10    4     pAnimTable         Animation table base pointer\n0x11    4     nDirection         Animation direction value\n0x12    4     dwStartTick        Animation start timestamp\n0x13    4     nCurrentFrame      Current frame index\n0x14    4     nAnimState         Animation state (0-4)\n0x15    4     dwPrimaryAlpha     Primary cel alpha value\n0x16    4     pfnStateCallback   Optional state change callback\n0x17    4     fAnimEnabled       Animation enabled flag\n\nAnimation Table Entry (16 bytes per state):\nOffset  Size  Field              Description\n0x00    4     ppCelPrimary       Pointer to primary cel pointer\n0x04    4     ppCelSecondary     Pointer to secondary cel pointer\n0x08    4     dwAlpha            Secondary cel alpha\n0x0C    4     nDirection         Direction for this state\n\nAnimation States:\n0 = Initial/Idle\n1 = Active (looping)\n2 = Playing forward (clamps at end, transitions to 3)\n3 = Stopped at end\n4 = Playing forward (clamps at end, transitions to 1)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x12 (18): Dwords to zero-initialize (72 bytes)\n- 0x10 (16): Animation table entry stride\n- 0x19 (25): Frame rate divisor (25 fps base)\n- 1000: Milliseconds per second for timing\n- 0xffffffff: Alpha parameter for GfxInterfaceCall84\n\nCalled From:\n- CreateGameObject stores this at field[7] as render callback",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
