      "name": "EditBoxCalcTextLayout",
      "signature": "void EditBoxCalcTextLayout(int * pEditData, int * pnCursorX, int * pnCursorY)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Calculate text layout and cursor position for edit box with text wrapping support.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate edit data structure and initialize local Unicode buffers\n2. Retrieve glyph width and current text dimensions from edit data\n3. Process text line by line, measuring width with unicode2Win and Ordinal_10122\n4. Track cursor position (X, Y) and detect wrapping boundaries\n5. Handle carriage return and newline characters for line breaks\n6. Return calculated cursor position via output parameters\n\nParameters:\n- pEditData (int*): Pointer to EditBox structure containing text, dimensions, and settings (offset +0x17=text, +0x97=cursor offset)\n- pnCursorX (int*): Output cursor X position\n- pnCursorY (int*): Output cursor Y position\n\nReturns:\n- void (results written to pnCursorX and pnCursorY)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x258 (600): Unicode buffer size for full text\n- 0x100 (256): Buffer size for line text conversion\n- 0x17 (23): Text pointer offset in EditBox structure\n- 0x97 (151): Cursor offset in EditBox structure\n- 0x9c: Font/glyph reference offset\n- 0x10, 0x11: Width/height field offsets",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
