      "name": "InitColorCodeToUnicode",
      "signature": "void InitColorCodeToUnicode(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Converts color code characters to Unicode format.\n\nClassification: Initialization - Sets up global Unicode color code data\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load base address of g_wsColorCode (0x6F9614E0)\n2. Set loop counter to 2 (two wide characters)\n3. Loop: Call toUnicode() to convert character at current position\n4. Increment position by 2 bytes (sizeof wchar_t)\n5. Decrement counter, repeat until done\n\nParameters: None (void)\n\nReturns: None (void)\n\nAssembly Analysis (from hex dump - function body truncated in Ghidra):\n  6f90b720: PUSH ESI\n  6f90b721: PUSH EDI  \n  6f90b722: MOV ESI, 0x6F9614E0  ; g_wsColorCode base\n  6f90b727: MOV EDI, 2           ; Loop count\n  6f90b72c: MOV ECX, ESI         ; param for toUnicode\n  6f90b72e: CALL [0x6F91D05C]    ; toUnicode import\n  6f90b734: ADD ESI, 2           ; Next wchar_t\n  6f90b737: DEC EDI              ; Decrement counter\n  6f90b738: JNZ loop             ; Continue if not zero\n  6f90b73a: POP EDI\n  6f90b73b: POP ESI\n  6f90b73c: RET\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function body appears truncated in Ghidra (shows only 1 byte)\n- Actual function spans 0x6f90b720-0x6f90b73c (29 bytes)\n- Requires function recreation to fix boundaries\n\nCalled From: Function pointer table at 0x6f91f008\nCalls: toUnicode (D2Lang import at 0x6F91D05C)",
