      "name": "CalcStringCharWidthSum",
      "signature": "int CalcStringCharWidthSum(short * pwString, int nMaxLength)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Calculates total character width for a string up to a maximum length.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize nTotalWidth and loop counter nIndex to 0\n2. Load first character from pwString array\n3. Check if character is null (0) or loop limit reached - if so, exit loop\n4. For each character, if not newline (0x0A), call DAT_6f9614e4 callback\n5. Callback returns character-specific width info at offset +3\n6. Accumulate all non-newline character widths into nTotalWidth\n7. Advance to next character in array, increment loop counter\n8. Return accumulated nTotalWidth sum\n\nParameters:\n- pwString (short*): Null-terminated array of character codes to measure\n- nMaxLength (int): Maximum number of characters to process\n\nReturns:\n- Total character width sum as int, 0 if empty string",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:35dea4a0051d7c449070481e8fdbd7f9",
