      "name": "ProcessUnicodeTextWithFormatting",
      "signature": "void ProcessUnicodeTextWithFormatting(ushort * pszText, int nX, int nY, int nCharIndex, int nMaxWidth, int nFontIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Processes Unicode text with special character formatting and font rendering.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize output buffer (18 dwords)\n2. Iterate through Unicode string characters\n3. For each character, check if it's escape sequence (0xFF) or newline (0x0A)\n4. Handle escape sequences via font processor callback\n5. Accumulate rendered dimensions (width, height)\n\nParameters:\n- pszText (Unicode*): Input Unicode string to process\n- nX (int): Starting X position\n- nY (int): Starting Y position\n- nCharIndex (int): Character index parameter\n- nMaxWidth (int): Maximum width limit or baseline width\n- nFontIndex (int): Font index for rendering\n\nReturns:\n- void (modifies output buffer and updates coordinates)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xFF: Escape sequence marker\n- 0x100: Character type boundary\n- 0x30: Digit character offset ('0')\n- 0x0C: Maximum digit value threshold\n- 0x0A: Newline character code\n- 0x14: Font handle structure stride\n- 0x10: Font advance scaling factor (divide by 16)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:2a02bab318a6cabacbd82d6501459656",
