      "name": "SetImageDataType",
      "signature": "void SetImageDataType(int * pImageData)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Validates and configures image data type field.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if pImageData[0] equals 2\n2. If not 2, trigger assertion failure with error location\n3. Set pImageData[0x11] (offset +68 bytes) to 5\n\nParameters:\n- pImageData (int *): Pointer to image data structure; pImageData[0] must equal 2\n\nReturns:\n- 1 on success (assertion passed and field set)\n\nNotes:\n- Assertion failure at D2Win.cpp:115 indicates invalid image type\n- Offset 0x11 (17) = 68 bytes into structure\n- Field value 5 likely represents IMAGETYPE_CONFIGURED state",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
