      "name": "MessagePumpLoop",
      "signature": "void MessagePumpLoop(void * pfnTickCallback)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Main message pump loop with periodic tick callback.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If enabled, enter message processing loop\n2. Peek for Windows messages; if none, execute tick callback at 25ms intervals\n3. If message exists, get message and dispatch it\n4. Check for exit condition (DAT_6f9216a8 == 0) to exit loop\n5. Final cleanup tick callback before returning\n\nParameters:\n- pfnTickCallback (void *): Function pointer called every ~25ms when idle\n- IMPLICIT: DAT_6f9216a8 controls loop state\n\nReturns:\n- 0 (always)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
