      "name": "RenderCompositeUnitFrames",
      "signature": "void RenderCompositeUnitFrames(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Prepare and render composite unit frames (inventory, party members, etc).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call message pump callback to initialize (Ordinal_10026)\n2. Iterate inventory nodes and invoke callback functions\n3. If current value is zero:\n   a. Reset data structures and prepare composite frame (Ordinal_10041)\n   b. Initialize global config buffer and fill with tile data via Ordinal_10072\n   c. Prepare and render all units in display list (Ordinal_10147/10148)\n   d. Render text and tooltips for each composite unit\n   e. Handle special inventory item updates\n   f. Render game state frame if applicable\n   g. Clean up freed inventory nodes\n4. Return void\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT: EBX contains context/environment pointer\n- No explicit parameters (called from MessagePumpLoop)\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Handles screen height/width validation\n- Processes callback depth to prevent reentrancy\n- Integrates with global config for frame rendering",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
