      "name": "MainWindowProc",
      "signature": "LRESULT MainWindowProc(HWND hWnd, uint uMsg, uint wParam, uint lParam)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "LRESULT",
      "comment": "Main Window Procedure - Handles Windows messages for the primary application window.\n\nClassification: Callback/Handler - Invoked by Windows for window messages\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if the system is initialized (g_dwInitialized). Return 0 if not initialized.\n2. If a custom message handler callback is set (g_dwCurrentValue), invoke it and return its result.\n3. Initialize result output variables (dwHandled, dwReturnValue) to 0.\n4. Handle WM_CLOSE (0x10): Set g_dwExitFlag to 1, post quit message, return 0.\n5. Dispatch message via DispatchWindowMessage for internal processing.\n6. If message was handled (nDispatchResult != 0) and dwHandled is set, return dwReturnValue.\n7. Fall through to DefWindowProcA for default Windows message processing.\n\nParameters:\n  hWnd (HWND, Stack[0x4]) - Handle to the window receiving the message\n  uMsg (uint, Stack[0x8]) - Message identifier (WM_* constant)\n  wParam (uint, Stack[0xc]) - Additional message-specific information\n  lParam (uint, Stack[0x10]) - Additional message-specific information\n\nReturns:\n  LRESULT - Message processing result:\n    - 0: For uninitialized state or WM_CLOSE\n    - Custom handler result if g_dwCurrentValue is set\n    - dwReturnValue if internal dispatch handled the message\n    - DefWindowProcA result for unhandled messages\n\nGlobals Referenced:\n  g_dwInitialized (0x6f961548) - System initialization flag\n  g_dwCurrentValue (0x6f961544) - Optional custom message handler callback\n  g_dwExitFlag (0x6f961560) - Application exit request flag\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x10 - WM_CLOSE message identifier\n\nCross-References:\n  Called from: InitializeGameDataChain (as WNDPROC callback registration)\n  Calls: DispatchWindowMessage, PostQuitMessage, DefWindowProcA",
