      "name": "ProcessClipboardOrInventoryCallbacks",
      "signature": "void ProcessClipboardOrInventoryCallbacks(int * pInputContext)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Processes clipboard input events or dispatches callbacks to inventory item handlers.\n\nClassification: Worker function - Dispatches input events through control chain\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If g_dwLastInputTime is set (pending input event):\n   a. If g_dwLastInventoryItem is null, process clipboard input directly\n   b. Otherwise traverse inventory linked list via +0x3c offset\n   c. If node matches g_dwLastInputTime, process clipboard input for that node\n   d. If clipboard processing succeeds (returns non-zero), skip to cache insertion\n2. If no pending input or clipboard processing failed:\n   a. Start from g_dwLastInventoryItem or g_pInventoryList\n   b. For each node with callback at offset +0x2c:\n      - Store node pointer in pInputContext[0]\n      - Increment g_nCallbackDepth (re-entrancy guard)\n      - Invoke callback with pInputContext\n      - Decrement g_nCallbackDepth\n      - If callback returns non-zero, stop iteration\n   c. Advance to next node via +0x3c offset\n3. Insert input context into cache via InsertCacheNodeWithCookie\n\nParameters:\n  pInputContext (int *, Stack[0x4]) - Input context structure:\n    +0x00: Current inventory item pointer (set during callback)\n    +0x08: Message parameter passed to EditBoxProcessClipboardInput\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nGlobals Referenced:\n  g_dwLastInputTime (0x6f961538) - Timestamp or ID of pending input event\n  g_dwLastInventoryItem (0x6f961540) - Head of active inventory item list\n  g_pInventoryList (0x6f961528) - Root of inventory item linked list\n  g_nCallbackDepth (0x6f961530) - Callback re-entrancy depth counter\n\nInventory Item Structure (partial):\n  +0x2c: Callback function pointer (code *)\n  +0x3c: Next item pointer in linked list (int *)\n\nSSA Variables (cannot be renamed):\n  iVar1 - Current node pointer during list traversal\n  iVar2 - Callback return value or next node pointer\n\nCross-References:\n  Calls: EditBoxProcessClipboardInput, InsertCacheNodeWithCookie\n  No direct callers - likely invoked via function pointer table",
