      "name": "ProcessInventoryItems",
      "signature": "void ProcessInventoryItems(InventoryItem * pItem)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Processes inventory items by invoking callbacks on linked list nodes.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if input time pointer and inventory item pointer are initialized\n2. If no last inventory item, invoke EditBoxKeyHandler with input data\n3. Otherwise, validate that last item exists in the linked list\n4. Iterate through inventory list starting from first item or cached item\n5. For each valid item node, check if callback function pointer is set (offset 0x30)\n6. If callback exists, increment callback depth counter and invoke callback with item pointer\n7. Decrement callback depth counter after callback returns\n8. Break iteration loop if callback returns non-zero success code\n9. Otherwise advance to next item via offset 0x3c and continue iteration\n10. Cache the processed item data using InsertCacheNodeWithCookie\n\nParameters:\n- pItem (InventoryItem*): Pointer to inventory item structure\n- IMPLICIT: EBX may contain context pointer (D2 calling convention)\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value; effects are through callbacks and global state updates)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x8: Data field offset within item structure\n- 0x30: Callback function pointer offset\n- 0x3c: Next node link offset\n\nRelated Functions:\n- EditBoxKeyHandler: Processes keyboard input\n- InsertCacheNodeWithCookie: Caches processed node data",
