      "name": "CaptureScreenshot",
      "signature": "void CaptureScreenshot(byte * pbPath, int nWidth, uint dwFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Captures screenshot to JPEG file at periodic intervals (1000ms+).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if 1000ms has elapsed since last screenshot\n2. Initialize JPEG encoder and allocate image buffer\n3. Generate screenshot filename based on counter\n4. Encode image using JPEG library\n5. Write encoded data to file\n6. Increment screenshot counter and free resources\n\nParameters:\n- pbPath (byte*): Output directory path for screenshot files\n- nWidth (int): Image width in pixels\n- dwFlags (uint): Encoding flags (0x80 = file_flag_write_through)\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nNotes:\n- Global g_dwLastScreenshotTime tracks last capture time\n- Global g_dwScreenshotCount tracks total screenshots captured\n- Throttled to 1000ms intervals to avoid excessive I/O",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:c5abbeac8cc844e821b083efaf175b39",
