      "name": "CaptureScreenshotToJpeg",
      "signature": "void CaptureScreenshotToJpeg(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "CaptureScreenshotToJpeg - Captures the game screen and saves it as a JPEG file.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Probe stack pages for large stack frame allocation (0x4F50 bytes)\n2. Call GetTickCount and check if 1000ms has elapsed since last screenshot\n3. If rate limit not met, set success flags and return early\n4. Call DispatchVirtualMethod to get screen dimensions (width/height)\n5. Allocate RGB pixel buffer via FogMemAlloc (width * height * 3 bytes)\n6. Call D2GFX Ordinal_10046 to capture screen contents to buffer\n7. If capture fails, skip to cleanup\n8. Loop to find unique filename:\n   a. Format filename as \"Screenshot%03d.jpg\" using screenshot counter\n   b. Increment g_dwScreenshotCount\n   c. Try CreateFileWrapper with OPEN_EXISTING to check if file exists\n   d. If file exists (handle != -1), close handle and continue loop\n   e. If file doesn't exist (handle == -1), exit loop with unique name\n9. Zero-initialize JPEG_CORE_PROPERTIES structure (0x1390 dwords = 0x4E40 bytes)\n10. Call ijlInit to initialize Intel JPEG Library structure\n11. Configure JPEG properties:\n    - Set pad bytes for row alignment (width*3 rounded up to 4-byte boundary minus width*3)\n    - Set output filename pointer\n    - Set image dimensions (width, height)\n    - Set color space indicator (1 = RGB)\n    - Set quality factor (100 = maximum quality)\n    - Set pixel buffer pointer\n12. Call ijlWrite with mode 8 (IJL_JFILE_WRITEWHOLEIMAGE) to encode and write JPEG\n13. Call ijlFree to release IJL resources\n14. Update g_dwLastScreenshotTime with current tick count\n15. Call ReleasePoolAllocation to free pixel buffer\n16. Set success flags in caller's context structure and return\n\nParameters:\n  None (uses global state for screen access)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Success indicated via flags at caller's context+0x18 and context+0x1C\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Rate limited to one screenshot per second (1000ms minimum interval)\n  - Screenshot counter wraps filename numbering (Screenshot000.jpg, Screenshot001.jpg, etc.)\n  - Files are not overwritten; counter increments until unique name found\n  - Maximum JPEG quality (100) used for best image fidelity\n\nGlobals Referenced:\n  g_dwLastScreenshotTime (0x6f961564) - Tick count of last screenshot\n  g_dwScreenshotCount (0x6f921554) - Running counter for unique filenames\n\nExternal Calls:\n  GetTickCount (KERNEL32) - Get current system tick count\n  D2GFX.Ordinal_10046 - Capture screen to RGB buffer\n  DispatchVirtualMethod (D2GFX) - Get screen dimensions\n  FogMemAlloc (FOG) - Allocate memory from pool\n  CreateFileWrapper (FOG) - Check file existence\n  CloseHandleWrapper (FOG) - Close file handle\n  ReleasePoolAllocation (FOG) - Free allocated memory\n  ijlInit, ijlWrite, ijlFree (IJL11) - Intel JPEG Library functions\n\nJPEG_CORE_PROPERTIES Structure (partial, at stack+0x10C):\n  Offset  Size  Field              Description\n  0x000   0x04  DIBBytes           Pointer to RGB pixel data\n  0x004   0x04  DIBWidth           Image width in pixels\n  0x008   0x04  DIBHeight          Image height in pixels\n  0x00C   0x04  DIBPadBytes        Row padding for 4-byte alignment\n  0x010   0x04  DIBChannels        Color channels (3 for RGB)\n  0x020   0x04  *JPGFile           Pointer to output filename string\n  0x02C   0x04  JPGWidth           Output JPEG width\n  0x030   0x04  JPGHeight          Output JPEG height\n  0x050   0x04  jquality           JPEG quality factor (1-100)\n\nNote: Function body boundaries corrupted in Ghidra - decompiler shows full code\nbut function body range shows only entry instruction. Stack frame is 0x4F50 bytes.",
