      "name": "RenderProgressBar",
      "signature": "int RenderProgressBar(int * pProgressBarData)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Renders a progress bar UI element by drawing a colored rectangle.\n\nClassification: Callback/Handler - render callback for D2WIN_PROGRESSBAR type (eType=10)\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pProgressBarData->eType == D2WIN_PROGRESSBAR (10), assert if invalid\n2. Check visibility flags at offset 0x8 against gdwBitMasks_exref[0] and gdwBitMasks_exref[2]\n3. If not visible, return 0 (nothing drawn)\n4. Find red color palette index via FindPaletteIndexForColor(0xff, 0, 0)\n5. Extract coordinates from progress bar structure:\n   - nMinX = pProgressBarData[3] (offset 0xC)\n   - nMinY = pProgressBarData[4] (offset 0x10)\n   - nMaxY = nMinY + pProgressBarData[6] (offset 0x18 = height)\n6. Calculate nMaxX using FPU value (progress percentage * width)\n7. Call GfxValidateClipCoordinates to draw clipped rectangle\n8. Return 1 (rendered successfully)\n\nParameters:\n- pProgressBarData (int * in ECX): Pointer to 0x44-byte progress bar structure\n  Offset 0x00: eType (must be 10 for D2WIN_PROGRESSBAR)\n  Offset 0x08: dwFlags (visibility bit flags)\n  Offset 0x0C: nMinX (left coordinate)\n  Offset 0x10: nMinY (top coordinate)\n  Offset 0x14: nWidth (bar width)\n  Offset 0x18: nHeight (bar height)\n  Offset 0x40: flProgress (float, current progress 0.0-1.0)\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Progress bar was rendered\n- 0: Progress bar not visible (flags not set)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Assert failure if eType != 10 (not a progress bar)\n- Returns 0 without rendering if visibility flags not set\n\nCaller Context:\n- Stored at offset 0x1C in progress bar object by AllocateAndInitializeObject\n- Called as render callback during UI draw cycle",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:4087a430c4c18c92ef786ff29281238b",
