      "name": "CleanupUnitType9",
      "signature": "int CleanupUnitType9(void * pUnit)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Validates and cleans up a unit of type 9, optionally deleting associated file.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Assert unit type equals 9 (type check)\n2. Call Ordinal_10038 at offset +0x140 (unit cleanup)\n3. If DAT_6f9cdba8 is 0, delete file at offset +0x10 (conditional file deletion)\n4. Return success (1)\n\nParameters:\n- pUnit (void*): Pointer to unit structure; first dword must equal 9 for type validation\n\nReturns:\n- 1 on success (always returns after cleanup operations)",
