      "name": "ValidateSmackDataAndInitGraphics",
      "signature": "dword ValidateSmackDataAndInitGraphics(int * pSmackData)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "Validates Smack video data structure and initializes graphics interface.\n\nKNOWN ISSUE: Function has incomplete boundaries in Ghidra (only entry byte 0x6f9112c0 \ndefined as function body). Decompiler follows code but formal variable/comment tracking \nis broken. Manual Ghidra intervention required to fix boundaries before full documentation.\n\nFunction Classification: Callback/Handler\n- Stored as function pointer in object[7] by CreateGameObjectByType\n- Single caller via function pointer table\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save current g_bySmackFileChar value to local (bySmackChar)\n2. Assert pSmackData->eType == 9 (SMACK type constant)\n   - If assertion fails: Call FogAssert then AssertFailure(0xFFFFFFFF) - no return\n3. Check dual bit mask condition on pSmackData[2] flags:\n   - Mask1: gdwBitMasks_exref[0] (offset +0)\n   - Mask2: gdwBitMasks_exref[2] (offset +8)\n   - Both masks must be set in flags, otherwise return 0\n4. If g_dwFileDeleteDisabled is non-zero (file operation pending):\n   a. If g_szSmackFilename is not empty (first char != '\\0'):\n      - Copy g_szSmackFilename to pSmackData+0x40 (filename buffer, 256 bytes)\n      - Call Ordinal_10038(pSmackData+0x140) - D2Gfx path resolution\n      - Call Ordinal_10036(pSmackData+0x40, pSmackData+0x140, EBP) - D2Gfx path combine\n      - Copy filename back to global (purpose unclear - possibly state sync)\n   b. Clear g_dwFileDeleteDisabled to 0\n5. Restore g_bySmackFileChar from saved value\n6. Call InitializeGraphicsInterface(pSmackData+0x140)\n7. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n- pSmackData (int* in ECX): Pointer to Smack video data structure (0x150 bytes)\n  - Offset 0x00: eType - Must be 9 for valid SMACK type\n  - Offset 0x08: dwFlags - Checked against gdwBitMasks for initialization conditions\n  - Offset 0x40: szFilename[256] - Video filename buffer\n  - Offset 0x140: GraphicsData - Graphics interface data (passed to init)\n\nReturns:\n- 1 (TRUE): Graphics interface initialized successfully\n- 0 (FALSE): Bit mask conditions not met, no initialization performed\n\nOrdinal Calls:\n- Ordinal_10038: D2Gfx - Resolves/prepares path buffer for file operation\n- Ordinal_10036: D2Gfx - Combines filename with resolved path (3 params)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Fatal assertion if eType != 9 (corrupt or wrong structure type)\n- unaff_EBP in decompiler indicates __fastcall with hidden 3rd parameter\n- File operations only occur when g_dwFileDeleteDisabled flag is set\n\nRelated Globals:\n- g_bySmackFileChar: Character state preserved across initialization\n- g_dwFileDeleteDisabled: Pending file delete flag (cleared after processing)\n- g_szSmackFilename: Current Smack video filename path\n- gdwBitMasks_exref: External bit mask table for flag validation\n\nMemory Model:\n- No allocations in this function\n- pSmackData ownership retained by caller (CreateGameObjectByType)",
