      "name": "CalculateTextBoxLineCount",
      "signature": "int CalculateTextBoxLineCount(int * pTextBox)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Calculate the number of lines of text that fit in a text box control.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pTextBox is non-null and type is 4 (textbox)\n2. Extract text dimensions from structure (nY at offset 0x11, nX at offset 0x6)\n3. Call Ordinal_10127 to get measured height\n4. Get system locale ID via GetLanguageLocaleId()\n5. If locale is 7 or 9 (CJK), set g_dwCJKFontHeight based on measured height threshold\n6. Calculate available height: (nX + nY * -2) - measured\n7. Divide by font height, add 1 for line count\n\nParameters:\n- pTextBox (int*): TextBox control structure; must be non-null and type=4\n\nReturns:\n- Line count that fits in text box (nX + nY*-2) / font_height + 1",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:938b064c6e0ca180ba1bc4087f7da3c2",
