      "name": "TextBoxGetLineChar",
      "signature": "dword TextBoxGetLineChar(int * ptTextData, int nLineNum, int nColumnNum)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "Retrieves a character from a specific line and column in a text box control.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate ptTextData pointer is not null\n2. Validate ptTextData->eType == 4 (TextBox type)\n3. Validate nLineNum < ptTextData->nNumLines\n4. Validate nColumnNum <= 4 (max columns)\n5. Traverse linked list of lines nLineNum times starting from ptTextData->ptFirstLine\n6. Validate final line pointer is not null\n7. Validate nLineCounter reached nLineNum (all lines traversed)\n8. Return character at offset [ptCurrentLine + nColumnNum * 4]\n\nParameters:\n- ptTextData (int*): Pointer to TextBox structure (eType must be 4)\n- nLineNum (int): Zero-based line number to retrieve from\n- nColumnNum (int): Zero-based column number (0-4)\n\nReturns:\n- dword: Character/value at the specified line and column position\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 4: TextBox type identifier (eType field)\n- 0x15: Offset to nNumLines field in TextBox structure\n- 0x12: Offset to ptFirstLine field in TextBox structure\n- 0x1c: Offset to ptNextLine field in line structure",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:783e31ab9c43deb8f76d198b8698243c",
