      "name": "CreateObjectInstance",
      "signature": "dword * CreateObjectInstance(dword nId, dword nCallback)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "dword *",
      "comment": "Allocates and initializes an object instance with a 72-byte (0x48) structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate memory for object (0x48 bytes)\n2. Initialize all fields to zero using REP STOSD\n3. Set initial state flags (field[0] = 8)\n4. Apply bit masks from global gdwBitMasks (offset +0/+8)\n5. Assign ID to field[0x10] and callback to field[0xd]\n6. Set vtable pointers at offsets 0x8 and 0xc\n7. Store tick count from GetTickCount at field[0x11]\n8. Link object into global object list\n\nParameters:\n- nId (ECX): Object identifier/handle\n- nCallback (EDX): Callback function pointer or state value\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to allocated and initialized object structure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x48 (72): Object structure size in bytes\n- 0x12 (18): DWORDs to clear during initialization\n- 0x8: Initial state value in field[0]\n- Offsets: 0xc, 0xd, 0x8, 0xf, 0x10, 0x11 map to structure fields",
