      "name": "ValidateTimerObjectState",
      "signature": "bool ValidateTimerObjectState(void * this)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Validates timer object state and optionally invokes callback based on elapsed time.\n\nNOTE: Function body incomplete in Ghidra - analysis from raw memory bytes.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Verify object state equals 8 (valid timer object marker)\n2. If state != 8, trigger assertion failure via FogAssert/AssertFailure\n3. Load global time data from address 0x6f91d164\n4. Check if object bit flags [+8] are set in global state [+8]\n5. If both flags clear, return 0 (no action needed)\n6. Call GetTickCount to get current system time\n7. Perform time calculation: (tick * 0x10624DD3) >> 6\n8. Compare calculated value with object field [+0x40]\n9. If time threshold exceeded and callback [+0x34] exists, invoke it\n10. Return 1 on success, 0 if conditions not met\n\nParameters:\n- this (ECX): Pointer to 72-byte TimerData structure (implicit __thiscall)\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Timer check succeeded, callback potentially invoked\n- 0: Timer conditions not met or object state invalid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Asserts if object state != 8 (corrupted or uninitialized object)\n- Skips callback if pfnCallback field is NULL\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 8: Valid object state marker\n- 0x10624DD3: Time scaling constant for tick conversion\n- 0x48 (72): TimerData structure size\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field           Description\n0x00    4     dwState         Object state marker (8 = valid)\n0x08    4     dwFlags         Bit flags from gdwBitMasks\n0x0c    4     pfnVtableFunc   Vtable function (FUN_6f913a20)\n0x0d    4     dwCallback      Callback function or state value\n0x10    4     nId             Object identifier\n0x11    4     dwTickCreated   GetTickCount at creation time\n0x34    4     pfnCallback     Callback function for timer expiry\n0x40    4     dwTimeValue     Time comparison value\n\nCalled From:\n- CreateObjectInstance assigns to pObject[8] as vtable method\n\nRelated:\n- FUN_6f913a20: Stored at pObject[0xc], similar validation\n- CreateObjectInstance: Creates/initializes timer object",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:cc74f9ebc8502b2ee9901491566d52ff",
