      "name": "LoadDataMpqFile",
      "signature": "uint * LoadDataMpqFile(int nMpqId, LPCSTR szMpqFile, int nUnknown1, int nUnknown2, uint dwFlags, int * pCallback, int nDelayMs)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "uint *",
      "comment": "Allocates and loads MPQ file data with retry logic and optional callback polling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0x108 bytes for data buffer via FogMemAlloc\n2. Loop: Call FUN_6f9140cb to load MPQ file data\n3. If load succeeds (non-zero status), return buffer\n4. If callback function provided (pCallback != NULL), call it\n5. If callback returns 0 or no callback, break and return NULL\n6. Sleep 100ms between retry attempts\n7. ReleasePoolAllocation on failure\n\nParameters:\n- nMpqId (int, ECX): MPQ identifier or mode\n- szMpqFile (LPCSTR, EDX): Path to MPQ file to load\n- nUnknown1 (int): Load flags or context parameter\n- nUnknown2 (int): Additional load parameter\n- dwFlags (uint): Operation flags (0x1ec seen in calls)\n- pCallback (int*): Optional callback function pointer to poll during wait\n- nDelayMs (int): Delay between retries (100ms sleep)\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to allocated uint buffer (0x108 bytes) on success\n- NULL if load fails and no callback returns success",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
