      "signature": "void FUN_6fd23482(double * pValue, char * szBuffer, size_t nSize, int nFormat)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Formats a double value to a decimal or exponential string representation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract mantissa and exponent from double via FUN_6f91888e\n2. Format mantissa digits with FUN_6f918817\n3. Determine if exponential format needed (exponent < -4 or >= size)\n4. If exponential: format with exponent using FormatExponentString\n5. If normal: adjust decimal point and format with FormatNumberString\n\nParameters:\n- pValue (double*): Pointer to double value to format\n- szBuffer (char*): Output buffer for formatted string\n- nSize (size_t): Maximum buffer size\n- nFormat (int): Format flags (precision/type)\n\nReturns:\n- void (string written to szBuffer)\n\nNotes:\n- local_2c: Temporary storage for mantissa digits (6 uint slots)\n- Register temporaries (EAX, EDI) used for intermediate calculations",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:466e27d82e265155c21adbf5b42c1734",
