      "name": "UpdateFpuControlBits",
      "signature": "uint UpdateFpuControlBits(void * this, void * pThis, dword dwMaskBits, dword dwSetBits)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Modifies specific bits in the floating point unit control word register.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save current FPU control word to stack using FSTCW instruction\n2. Combine saved control word with upper 16 bits of context pointer into composite value\n3. Retrieve current FPU control word value via GetFpuControlWord()\n4. Apply bit mask operation: (current & ~dwBitMask) | (dwNewBits & dwBitMask)\n5. Set updated FPU control word via SetFpuControlWord()\n6. Restore original FPU control word from stack using FLDCW instruction\n7. Return the updated control word value\n\nParameters:\n- this (void*): Context pointer (upper 16 bits used in composite value)\n- dwNewBits (uint): New bit values to apply where mask is set\n- dwBitMask (uint): Bit mask indicating which bits to modify (1=modify, 0=preserve)\n\nReturns:\n- uint: Updated FPU control word value after applying bit modifications\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If dwBitMask is 0x0000, function returns current control word unchanged\n- If dwBitMask is 0xFFFF, function returns dwNewBits (full replacement)\n- IMPLICIT: Original FPU control word is preserved and restored\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x10: Bit shift for extracting upper 16 bits of context pointer\n- FSTCW: Store FPU Control Word (saves current state)\n- FLDCW: Load FPU Control Word (restores saved state)\n\nError Handling:\n- Function assumes valid context pointer and control word operations\n- No validation of bit mask or new bit values\n- FPU control word operations are atomic at instruction level",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:d66e712fbac3885aa0ffabe41c913eb0",
