      "name": "AddUintWithOverflowCheck",
      "signature": "uint AddUintWithOverflowCheck(uint dwOperand1, uint dwOperand2, uint * pdwResult)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Adds two unsigned integers with overflow detection.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize overflow flag to 0 (no overflow)\n2. Calculate sum = dwOperand1 + dwOperand2\n3. Check for overflow conditions: sum < dwOperand1 OR sum < dwOperand2\n4. If overflow detected, set overflow flag to 1\n5. Store sum result in output parameter pdwResult\n6. Return overflow flag (0 = success, 1 = overflow)\n\nParameters:\n  dwOperand1 - First unsigned integer operand\n  dwOperand2 - Second unsigned integer operand  \n  pdwResult - Pointer to store the addition result\n\nReturns:\n  0 - Addition successful, no overflow occurred\n  1 - Overflow detected during addition\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Overflow detection uses standard method: if result is less than either operand,\n  overflow occurred. This works because unsigned arithmetic wraps around on overflow.\n\nError Handling:\n  No error handling for null pointer - assumes pdwResult is valid.\n  Overflow is detected but does not prevent result storage.",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
